<title>USA: Kennedy plan to raise U.S. cigarette tax defeated.</title>
<headline>Kennedy plan to raise U.S. cigarette tax defeated.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Senate on Friday defeated an amendment offered by Sen. Edward Kennedy to increase the cigarette tax by 23 cents per pack to pay for children's health programs.</p>
<p>The tax would have been in addition to the 20-cent per pack cigarette tax increase already in the tax bill being considered by the Senate. The current federal cigarette tax is 24 cents per pack.</p>
<p>Kennedy, a Massachusetts Democrat, released a letter Thursday from Health and Human Services Secretary Donna Shalala saying the administration supported his proposal.</p>
<p>((--Washington Newsroom 202 898-8300))</p>
